Isaiah	Is	27	57	10	Thou hast been wearied in the multitude of thy ways: yet thou saidst not: I will rest: thou hast found life of thy hand, therefore thou hast not asked.
Isaiah	Is	27	57	11	For whom hast thou been solicitous and afraid, that thou hast lied, and hast not been mindful of me, nor thought on me in thy heart? for I am silent, and as one that seeth not, and thou hast forgotten me.
Isaiah	Is	27	57	12	I will declare thy justice, and thy works shall not profit thee.
