Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	16	Say ye to the nations: Behold it is heard in Jerusalem, that guards are coming from a far country, and give out their voice against the cities of Juda.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	17	They are set round about her, as keepers of fields: because she hath provoked me to wrath, saith the Lord.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	18	Thy ways, and thy devices have brought these things upon thee: this is thy wickedness, because it is bitter, because it hath touched thy heart.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	19	My bowels, my bowels are in pain, the senses of my heart are troubled within me, I will not hold my peace, for my soul hath heard the sound of the trumpet, the cry of battle.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	20	Destruction upon destruction is called for, and all the earth is laid waste: my tents are destroyed on a sudden, and my pavilions in a moment.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	21	How long shall I see men fleeing away, how long shall I hear the sound of the trumpet?
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	22	For my foolish people have not known me: they are foolish and senseless children: they are wise to do evil, but to do good they have no knowledge.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	23	I beheld the earth, and lo it was void, and nothing: and the heavens, and there was no light in them.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	24	I looked upon the mountains, and behold they trembled: and all the hills were troubled.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	25	I beheld, and lo there was no man: and all the birds of the air were gone.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	26	I looked, and behold Carmel was a wilderness: and all its cities were destroyed at the presence of the Lord, and at the presence of the wrath of his indignation.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	27	For thus saith the Lord: All the land shall be desolate, but yet I will not utterly destroy.
