Jeremiah	Jer	28	4	31	For I have heard the voice as of a woman in travail, anguishes as of a woman in labor of a child. The voice of the daughter of Sion, dying away, spreading her hands: Woe is me, for my soul hath fainted because of them that are slain.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	1	Go about through the streets of Jerusalem, and see, and consider, and seek in the broad places thereof, if you can find a man that executeth judgment, and seeketh faith: and I will be merciful unto it.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	2	And though they say: The Lord liveth; this also they will swear falsely.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	3	O Lord, thy eyes are upon truth: thou hast struck them, and they have not grieved: thou hast bruised them, and they have refused to receive correction: they have made their faces harder than the rock, and they have refused to return.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	4	But I said: Perhaps these are poor and foolish, that know not the way of the Lord, the judgment of their God.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	5	I will go therefore to the great men, and I will speak to them: for they know the way of the Lord, the judgment of their God: and behold these have together broken the yoke more, and have burst the bonds.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	6	Wherefore a lion out of the wood hath slain them, a wolf in the evening, hath spoiled them, a leopard watcheth for their cities: every one that shall go out thence shall be taken, because their transgressions are multiplied, their rebellions are strengthened.
