Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	18	Nevertheless in those days, saith the Lord, I will not bring you to utter destruction.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	19	And if you shall say: why hath the Lord our God done all these things to us? Thou shalt say to them: As you have forsaken me, and served a strange god in your own land, so shall you serve strangers in a land that is not your own.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	20	Declare ye this to the house of Jacob, and publish it in Juda, saying:
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	21	Hear, O foolish people, and without understanding: who have eyes, and see not: and ears, and hear not.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	22	Will not you then fear me, saith the Lord: and will you not repent at my presence? I have set the sand a bound for the sea, an everlasting ordinance, which it shall not pass over: and the waves thereof shall toss themselves, and shall not prevail: they shall swell, and shall not pass over it.
Jeremiah	Jer	28	5	23	But the heart of this people is become hard of belief and provoking, they are revolted and gone away.
